<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Province of New York</h1><p class="st-meta">1664 CE – 1776 CE · capital New York</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The English colony created from Dutch New Netherland in 1664, whose port grew into the commercial heart of British North America.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1664 an English fleet under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-nicolls">Richard Nicolls</a> seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-amsterdam">New Amsterdam</a>, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-of-england">Charles II</a> had granted to his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-england">James, Duke of York</a>. The colony was renamed after James, who ruled it as proprietor through governors under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dukes-laws">Duke's Laws</a> of 1665. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> briefly recaptured it in 1673 to 1674.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>When James became king in 1685, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> became a royal province, and in 1688 it was folded into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dominion-of-new-england">Dominion of New England</a>. Its collapse triggered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leislers-rebellion">Leisler's Rebellion</a> of 1689 to 1691. A large landholding elite owned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudson-valley">Hudson Valley</a> manors, and New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york-maine">York</a> City grew as a trading port with many enslaved Africans. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-peter-zenger">Zenger</a> trial of 1735 advanced press freedom, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albany-congress">Albany Congress</a> of 1754 met there. Alliance with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/iroquois-confederacy">Iroquois Confederacy</a> shaped frontier policy.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York City</a> hosted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stamp-act-congress">Stamp Act Congress</a> in 1765. In July 1776 the provincial congress endorsed independence and New York became a state of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a>, though British forces occupied New York City until 1783.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/province-of-new-york.jpg" alt="Province of New York" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: AnonMoos, based on image by Zscout370, AnonMoos · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_ensign_of_Great_Britain_(1707%E2%80%931800,_square_canton).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1664 CE – 1776 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>New York</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Richard Nicolls, Edmund Andros, William Tryon</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Anglicanism, Dutch Reformed Church</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>New York (colony)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1720&amp;focus=province-of-new-york" aria-label="Province of New York on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2866 724 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Province of New York lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3186 980L3186 980M3186 980L4970 663M3186 980L3277 927M3186 980L4997 651M3186 980L2570 1008M3186 980L3136 1013"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3186 980h0M4970 663h0M3277 927h0M4997 651h0M2570 1008h0M3136 1013h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3186 980h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3186 980h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1720&amp;focus=province-of-new-york">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
